You are right. v9 still built a lists folder in patches 3 to 8 and
only removed it in patch 9. It also took quarantine as a fifth folder,
from your list in "Re: [PATCH v3 0/8] jails/instances/lab-mail: Build
the list's mail hub" [1].

v10 is posted as "[PATCH v10 00/10] jails/instances/lab-mail: Build
the list's mail hub" [2], and lists never appears in it. A new
patch 3 moves the list into INBOX in the spec first. The steps after
it build on INBOX from the start. The folders are INBOX, Next, Later,
and Archive, and nothing else.

> Only those should sync, so that I can create additional dirs on Fastmail
> and not have them show up in notmuch.

Done. lab-mail's mbsync now has "Patterns INBOX Next Later Archive"
with "Create None", and mbsync no longer has the ACL's create right.
A folder you make on Fastmail stays there, and reaches neither
lab-mail nor any client. v9 synced every folder because [1] said "I
want lab-mail to sync all folders with fastmail". I took this message
as replacing that.

Before deploying, delete the Fastmail rule that files list mail into
lists, and create Next and Later on Fastmail, since mbsync creates no
folder. Anything still in lists on Fastmail stays there until you move
it.

quarantine is not a lab-mail folder now. "[PATCH 0/2] Quarantine mail
from unapproved senders" [3] files quarantined mail under quarantine/
in the jj maildir, so it does not depend on this series. Once
lab-process-mail reads from lab-mail instead, quarantined mail will
need a home. My recommendation is a Dovecot folder on lab-mail that is
not synced to Fastmail. That can wait until then.

